epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/03-archive-read-and-reopen-surface.md:5:Expose process archive reads through authenticated Fastify routes and client surfaces so finalized entries remain visible after reload or environment loss.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/03-archive-read-and-reopen-surface.md:18:Add process archive read routes and user-visible archive rendering that read durable canonical entries, enforce project/process access, show empty states, and display degraded entries without hiding healthy entries.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/03-archive-read-and-reopen-surface.md:28:- `ArchiveReadService.getArchive`\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/03-archive-read-and-reopen-surface.md:71:  - When: User opens the process archive\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/03-archive-read-and-reopen-surface.md:78:  - When: User requests a process archive from that project\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/03-archive-read-and-reopen-surface.md:80:- **TC-3.3b: Missing process archive read returns not found**\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/03-archive-read-and-reopen-surface.md:82:  - When: User requests the process archive\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/03-archive-read-and-reopen-surface.md:106:| Get process archive | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/archive` | Returns finalized canonical archive entries for one process |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/03-archive-read-and-reopen-surface.md:135:| Process/archive UI entry | `apps/platform/client/features/processes/archive-section.ts`, `apps/platform/client/app/bootstrap.ts` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/03-archive-read-and-reopen-surface.md:140:- Archive reads depend on durable `archiveEntries`, not live WebSocket state or environment state.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/03-archive-read-and-reopen-surface.md:141:- `ArchiveReadService` returns a bounded page of canonical archive entries for the route and preserves any per-entry degraded status present on the response contract.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/03-archive-read-and-reopen-surface.md:147:- [tech-design.md](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:404), lines 404-442\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/03-archive-read-and-reopen-surface.md:148:- [tech-design.md](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:602), lines 602-613\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/03-archive-read-and-reopen-surface.md:149:- [test-plan.md](/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md:50), lines 50-56\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/03-archive-read-and-reopen-surface.md:155:| TC-3.1a | `tests/service/client/archive-section.test.ts` | archive entries visible |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/03-archive-read-and-reopen-surface.md:156:| TC-3.1b | `tests/service/client/archive-section.test.ts` | empty archive state visible |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/stories/03-archive-read-and-reopen-surface.md:160:| TC-3.3b | `tests/service/server/archive-api.test.ts` | missing process archive read returns not found |\n./apps/platform/client/features/processes/archive-section.ts:54:  section.setAttribute('data-archive-section', 'true');\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:6:process archive, turn derivation, and non-summarizing structural derived views.\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:19:- Epic: `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/epic.md`\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:20:- Test plan: `docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/test-plan.md`\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:38:| Current `processHistoryItems` vocabulary differs from canonical archive taxonomy | Baseline, Tech Design Question 2 | Design adds new `archiveEntries` while bridging current history for compatibility. No historical migration/backfill is included. | Resolved - clarified |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:39:| Finalization boundary must prevent raw deltas and interrupted partial objects | AC-2.x, Tech Design Question 3 | Design introduces `ArchiveFinalizationService` and `finalizationKey` idempotency. Only completed objects call append. | Resolved |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:40:| Turn and derived-view persistence could accidentally become canonical truth | AC-4.x, AC-5.x | Design treats turns and derived views as cached/rebuildable projections over `archiveEntries`. | Resolved |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:53:| 1 | What durable schema stores archive entries, sequence numbers, related references, and idempotency keys? | Add `archiveEntries` with `projectId`, `processId`, `entryKind`, `sequence`, `finalizationKey`, `sourceObjectId`, body fields, related ids, status, and timestamps. Convex assigns sequence inside an append mutation and enforces `finalizationKey` idempotency per process. |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:55:| 3 | What finalization boundary determines when entries are archived? | `ArchiveFinalizationService` is called only from completion points: accepted user responses, completed model/runtime objects, completed script emissions, finalized tool calls/results, and process events. Raw live deltas and interrupted partial objects never call append. |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:57:| 5 | Should turns be persisted, computed on read, or cached with rebuild? | Turns are cached derived records in `archiveTurns` for bounded reads, but they are rebuildable from `archiveEntries` and never canonical truth. |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:58:| 6 | What minimal derived-view representation should Epic 7 implement? | Implement structural `turn_range` and `chunk_candidate` views with source turn/archive ids, optional labels, and status metadata. No model-generated summaries or summarization prompts. |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:60:| 8 | What pagination/indexing keeps reads bounded? | Convex indexes `archiveEntries` by `processId, sequence`, `archiveTurns` by `processId, turnIndex`, and derived views by `processId, updatedAt`. Fastify routes expose cursor pagination and default page limits. |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:61:| 9 | What idempotency strategy prevents duplicate archive entries? | `appendArchiveEntry` checks `processId + finalizationKey`. A replay returns the existing entry or no-ops. Sequence assignment happens only on first append. |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:108:    FINAL[ArchiveFinalizationService]\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:111:    READ[ArchiveReadService]\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:112:    DERIVE[TurnDerivationService]\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:113:    VIEWS[DerivedArchiveViewService]\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:129:`ArchiveFinalizationService` when a process object is complete. The service\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:133:The read path is broader. Fastify routes call `ArchiveReadService` for archive\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:134:entries, `TurnDerivationService` for turns, and `DerivedArchiveViewService` for\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:143:| Add new `archiveEntries` instead of replacing `processHistoryItems` | Current history is presentation-oriented and already used by live process surfaces | Epic 7 can preserve archive truth without destabilizing current UI |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:146:| Turns are cached projections | Long processes need bounded turn reads, but turns are derived | `archiveTurns` can be rebuilt from `archiveEntries` |\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:157:├── archiveEntries.ts                         # NEW: append/read canonical archive entries\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:158:├── archiveTurns.ts                           # NEW: cached derived turn records\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:159:├── derivedArchiveViews.ts                    # NEW: structural derived-view records\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:163:├── archive.ts                                # NEW: archive/turn/derived-view contracts and route builders\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:171:└── archive.ts                                # NEW: authenticated archive/turn/derived-view routes\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:189:├── archive-section.ts                        # NEW: process archive read surface\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/07--archive-and-derived-views/tech-design.md:191:└── derived-archive-views-section.ts          # NEW: structural derived-view surface\n./d